IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa18-part22-interest`

-- coa18-part22-register.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 22, ss 808 to 819: the register of interests
-- disclosed, its index, the rights to inspect and to a copy, court supervision of the purpose, the offences, the removal
-- and adjustment of entries, and the duty of a company that ceases to be public. Lines 10933-11034 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. How to read an answer (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, NOTHING), the gate of s 791 and the
-- seams are as in the header of coa18-part22-notice.l4. Periods of days are in working days (s 827): the functions that
-- carry one take the count of working days elapsed as an input.

§ `Part 22 (ss 791 to 828), second module: ss 808 to 819`

§§ `s 808 Register of interests disclosed`

-- src:10934 | 808 Register of interests disclosed
-- src:10935 | (1) The company must keep a register of information received by it in pursuance of a requirement imposed under section 793 (notice requiring information about interests in company's shares).
@ref s 808(1) Register of interests disclosed (src:10934-10935)
GIVEN `information has been received by the company in pursuance of a requirement imposed under section 793` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 808(1) the company must keep a register of the information received` MEANS
    IF `information has been received by the company in pursuance of a requirement imposed under section 793`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a register of information received by it in pursuance of a requirement imposed under section 793": a company that has received none is not mentioned

@ref s 808(1) Register of interests disclosed (src:10935-10935)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 808(1) the company must keep a register of the information received` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST (`Action of a party` OF Company, Company, "s 808(1) keeps a register of the information received in pursuance of a requirement imposed under section 793")
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 808(1): no register of the information received under section 793 was kept"

-- src:10936 | (2) A company which receives any such information must, within three days of the receipt, enter in the register—
-- src:10937 | (a) the fact that the requirement was imposed and the date on which it was imposed, and
-- src:10938 | (b) the information received in pursuance of the requirement.
@ref s 808(2) Register of interests disclosed (src:10936-10938)
GIVEN `the number of working days, reckoned under section 827, from the receipt of the information to the entry in the register` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 808(2) the company entered the information in the register within three days of the receipt` MEANS
    IF `the number of working days, reckoned under section 827, from the receipt of the information to the entry in the register` AT MOST 3
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company which receives any such information must, within three days of the receipt, enter in the register"

@ref s 808(2)(a) Register of interests disclosed (src:10937-10938)
GIVEN `the entry records the fact that the requirement was imposed and the date on which it was imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entry records the information received in pursuance of the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 808(2)(a) the entry contains the particulars the company must enter` MEANS
    IF `the entry records the fact that the requirement was imposed and the date on which it was imposed` AND `the entry records the information received in pursuance of the requirement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must ... enter in the register— (a) the fact that the requirement was imposed and the date on which it was imposed, and (b) the information received in pursuance of the requirement": a required particular is missing, so the entry does not contain what the company must enter

@ref s 808(2) Register of interests disclosed (src:10936-10938)
GIVEN `the day on which the information was received` IS A DATE
      `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`s 808(2) the last day for entering the information in the register` MEANS
    `s 827 the last day of a period of days counting only working days` `the day on which the information was received` 3 `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company`

@ref s 808(2) Register of interests disclosed (src:10936-10938)
GIVEN `the number of days allowed, reckoned under section 827` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 808(2) the company that receives the information must enter it in the register within three days of the receipt` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST (`Action of a party` OF Company, Company, "s 808(2) enters in the register the fact that the requirement was imposed, its date and the information received")
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed, reckoned under section 827`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 808(2): the information was not entered in the register within three days of the receipt"

-- (3): entered against the name of the present holder or, if there is none or he is not known, against the name of the
-- person holding the interest.
-- src:10939 | (3) The information must be entered against the name of the present holder of the shares in question or, if there is no present holder or the present holder is not known, against the name of the person holding the interest.
@ref s 808(3) Register of interests disclosed (src:10939-10939)
GIVEN `there is a present holder of the shares in question and he is known` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is entered against the name of the present holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is entered against the name of the person holding the interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 808(3) the information is entered against the name the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `there is a present holder of the shares in question and he is known`
    THEN IF `the information is entered against the name of the present holder`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The information must be entered against the name of the present holder of the shares in question"
    ELSE IF `the information is entered against the name of the person holding the interest`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or, if there is no present holder or the present holder is not known, against the name of the person holding the interest"

-- src:10940 | (4) The register must be made up so that the entries against the names entered in it appear in chronological order.
@ref s 808(4) Register of interests disclosed (src:10940-10940)
GIVEN `the entries against the names entered in the register appear in chronological order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 808(4) the register is made up as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the entries against the names entered in the register appear in chronological order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The register must be made up so that the entries against the names entered in it appear in chronological order."

-- src:10941 | (5) If default is made in complying with this section an offence is committed by—
-- src:10942 | (a) the company, and
-- src:10943 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 808(5) Register of interests disclosed (src:10941-10943)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 808` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 808(5)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 808`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section an offence is committed by— (a) the company"

@ref s 808(5)(b) Register of interests disclosed (src:10943-10943)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 808` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 808(5)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 808`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default` -- JUST FALSE here is the text's "who is in default"; NOTHING stays NOTHING (points outside the text, s 1121)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section an offence is committed by— ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default."

-- src:10944 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 808(6) Register of interests disclosed (src:10944-10944)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 808(6) the penalty on summary conviction` MEANS
    --                         how convicted,                imprisonment not exceeding, fine not exceeding,                                           daily default fine,                                                    imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on summary conviction`                      THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`,                      NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland`          THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`,          NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`  THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`,  NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says only "on summary conviction"; a conviction on indictment is not mentioned

-- src:10945 | (7) The company is not by virtue of anything done for the purposes of this section affected with notice of, or put upon inquiry as to, the rights of any person in relation to any shares.
@ref s 808(7) Register of interests disclosed (src:10945-10945)
GIVEN `the thing was done for the purposes of section 808` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 808(7) the company is affected with notice of, or put upon inquiry as to, the rights of any person in relation to any shares` MEANS
    IF `the thing was done for the purposes of section 808`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company is not by virtue of anything done for the purposes of this section affected with notice of, or put upon inquiry as to, the rights of any person in relation to any shares."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by virtue of anything done for the purposes of this section": notice by other means is not mentioned

§§ `s 809 Register to be kept available for inspection`

-- src:10947 | (1) The register kept under section 808 (register of interests disclosed) must be kept available for inspection—
-- src:10948 | (a) at the company's registered office, or
-- src:10949 | (b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136.
@ref s 809(1) Register to be kept available for inspection (src:10947-10949)
GIVEN `the register is kept available for inspection at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1136 the place is specified in regulations under section 1136` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 809(1) the place at which the register is kept available for inspection is a place the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `the register is kept available for inspection at the company's registered office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `s 1136 the place is specified in regulations under section 1136` -- JUST FALSE is the seam's own no ("(b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136"); NOTHING stays NOTHING (points outside the text)

-- (3) is a "no notice is required if ..." rule; (2) calls it.
-- src:10951 | (3) No such notice is required if the register has at all times been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office.
@ref s 809(3) Register to be kept available for inspection (src:10951-10951)
GIVEN `the register has at all times been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 809(3) no such notice is required` MEANS
    IF `the register has at all times been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No such notice is required if the register has at all times been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office."

-- src:10950 | (2) A company must give notice to the registrar of companies of the place where the register is kept available for inspection and of any change in that place.
@ref s 809(2) Register to be kept available for inspection (src:10950-10950)
GIVEN `the register has at all times been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 809(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of companies of the place where the register is kept and of any change in that place` MEANS
    IF `s 809(3) no such notice is required` `the register has at all times been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(3) No such notice is required if the register has at all times been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office."
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 809(2) Register to be kept available for inspection (src:10950-10950)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 809(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place where the register is kept` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST (`Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "s 809(2) gives notice of the place where the register is kept available for inspection and of any change in that place")
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 809(2): notice of the place of the register was not given to the registrar"

-- src:10952 | (4) If default is made in complying with subsection (1), or a company makes default for 14 days in complying with subsection (2), an offence is committed by—
-- src:10953 | (a) the company, and
-- src:10954 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 809(4) Register to be kept available for inspection (src:10952-10954)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company makes default for 14 days in complying with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 809(4)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` OR `the company makes default for 14 days in complying with subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (1), or a company makes default for 14 days in complying with subsection (2), an offence is committed by— (a) the company"

@ref s 809(4)(b) Register to be kept available for inspection (src:10954-10954)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company makes default for 14 days in complying with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 809(4)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` OR `the company makes default for 14 days in complying with subsection (2)`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default` -- JUST FALSE here is the text's "who is in default"; NOTHING stays NOTHING (points outside the text, s 1121)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (1), or a company makes default for 14 days in complying with subsection (2), an offence is committed by— ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default."

-- src:10955 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 809(5) Register to be kept available for inspection (src:10955-10955)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 809(5) the penalty on summary conviction` MEANS
    --                         how convicted,                imprisonment not exceeding, fine not exceeding,                                           daily default fine,                                                    imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on summary conviction`                      THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`,                      NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland`          THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`,          NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`  THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`,  NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says only "on summary conviction"; a conviction on indictment is not mentioned

§§ `s 810 Associated index`

-- src:10957 | (1) Unless the register kept under section 808 (register of interests disclosed) is kept in such a form as itself to constitute an index, the company must keep an index of the names entered in it.
@ref s 810(1) Associated index (src:10957-10957)
GIVEN `the register is kept in such a form as itself to constitute an index` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810(1) the company must keep an index of the names entered in the register` MEANS
    IF `the register is kept in such a form as itself to constitute an index`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the register kept under section 808 ... is kept in such a form as itself to constitute an index, the company must keep an index of the names entered in it."
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 810(1) Associated index (src:10957-10957)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 810(1) the company must keep an index of the names entered in the register` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST (`Action of a party` OF Company, Company, "s 810(1) keeps an index of the names entered in the register")
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 810(1): no index of the names entered in the register was kept"

-- src:10958 | (2) The company must make any necessary entry or alteration in the index within ten days after the date on which any entry or alteration is made in the register.
@ref s 810(2) Associated index (src:10958-10958)
GIVEN `the number of working days, reckoned under section 827, from the entry or alteration in the register to the entry or alteration in the index` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810(2) the company made the entry or alteration in the index within ten days` MEANS
    IF `the number of working days, reckoned under section 827, from the entry or alteration in the register to the entry or alteration in the index` AT MOST 10
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must make any necessary entry or alteration in the index within ten days after the date on which any entry or alteration is made in the register."

@ref s 810(2) Associated index (src:10958-10958)
GIVEN `the day on which the entry or alteration was made in the register` IS A DATE
      `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`s 810(2) the last day for making the entry or alteration in the index` MEANS
    `s 827 the last day of a period of days counting only working days` `the day on which the entry or alteration was made in the register` 10 `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company`

@ref s 810(2) Associated index (src:10958-10958)
GIVEN `the number of days allowed, reckoned under section 827` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 810(2) the company must make any necessary entry or alteration in the index within ten days` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST (`Action of a party` OF Company, Company, "s 810(2) makes the necessary entry or alteration in the index")
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed, reckoned under section 827`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 810(2): the entry or alteration was not made in the index within ten days"

-- src:10959 | (3) The index must contain, in respect of each name, a sufficient indication to enable the information entered against it to be readily found.
@ref s 810(3) Associated index (src:10959-10959)
GIVEN `the index contains, in respect of each name, a sufficient indication to enable the information entered against it to be readily found` IS A BOOLEAN
