`s 810(3) the index is made up as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the index contains, in respect of each name, a sufficient indication to enable the information entered against it to be readily found`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The index must contain, in respect of each name, a sufficient indication to enable the information entered against it to be readily found."

-- src:10960 | (4) The index must be at all times kept available for inspection at the same place as the register.
