-- src:10964 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 810(6) Associated index (src:10964-10964)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 810(6) the penalty on summary conviction` MEANS
    --                         how convicted,                imprisonment not exceeding, fine not exceeding,                                           daily default fine,                                                    imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on summary conviction`                      THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`,                      NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland`          THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`,          NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`  THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`,  NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says only "on summary conviction"; a conviction on indictment is not mentioned

§§ `s 811 Rights to inspect and require copy of entries`

-- src:10966 | (1) The register required to be kept under section 808 (register of interests disclosed), and any associated index, must be open to inspection by any person without charge.
@ref s 811(1) Rights to inspect and require copy of entries (src:10966-10966)
GIVEN `the document is the register required to be kept under section 808 or an associated index` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 811(1) the document must be open to inspection by any person without charge` MEANS
    IF `the document is the register required to be kept under section 808 or an associated index`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The register required to be kept under section 808 ..., and any associated index, must be open to inspection by any person without charge."

-- src:10967 | (2) Any person is entitled, on request and on payment of such fee as may be prescribed, to be provided with a copy of any entry in the register.
@ref s 811(2) Rights to inspect and require copy of entries (src:10967-10967)
GIVEN `the person has made a request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has paid such fee as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 811(2) the person is entitled to be provided with a copy of any entry in the register` MEANS
    IF `the person has made a request` AND `the person has paid such fee as may be prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any person is entitled, on request and on payment of such fee as may be prescribed, to be provided with a copy of any entry in the register." ("on" counts as "where")

-- src:10968 | (3) A person seeking to exercise either of the rights conferred by this section must make a request to the company to that effect.
@ref s 811(3) Rights to inspect and require copy of entries (src:10968-10968)
GIVEN `the person has made a request to the company to that effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 811(3) the person has made the request the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the person has made a request to the company to that effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person seeking to exercise either of the rights conferred by this section must make a request to the company to that effect."

-- (4): what the request must contain. The requester is an individual or an organisation; the information may be
-- disclosed to another person, who is again an individual or an organisation.
DECLARE `s 811(4) kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `s 811(4) an individual`
    `s 811(4) an organisation`

-- src:10969 | (4) The request must contain the following information—
-- src:10970 | (a) in the case of an individual, his name and address;
-- src:10971 | (b) in the case of an organisation, the name and address of an individual responsible for making the request on behalf of the organisation;
-- src:10972 | (c) the purpose for which the information is to be used; and
-- src:10973 | (d) whether the information will be disclosed to any other person, and if so—
-- src:10974 | (i) where that person is an individual, his name and address,
-- src:10975 | (ii) where that person is an organisation, the name and address of an individual responsible for receiving the information on its behalf, and
-- src:10976 | (iii) the purpose for which the information is to be used by that person.
@ref s 811(4) Rights to inspect and require copy of entries (src:10969-10976)
GIVEN `the requester` IS A `s 811(4) kind of person`
      `the request gives the requester's name and address, or for an organisation the name and address of an individual responsible for making the request on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request states the purpose for which the information is to be used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request states whether the information will be disclosed to any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information will be disclosed to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person` IS A `s 811(4) kind of person`
      `the request gives the other person's name and address, or for an organisation the name and address of an individual responsible for receiving the information on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request states the purpose for which the other person is to use the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 811(4) the request contains the information the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF     `the request gives the requester's name and address, or for an organisation the name and address of an individual responsible for making the request on its behalf`
       AND `the request states the purpose for which the information is to be used`
       AND `the request states whether the information will be disclosed to any other person`
       AND (   (NOT `the information will be disclosed to another person`)
            OR (    `the request gives the other person's name and address, or for an organisation the name and address of an individual responsible for receiving the information on its behalf`
                AND `the request states the purpose for which the other person is to use the information`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The request must contain the following information— (a) in the case of an individual, his name and address; (b) in the case of an organisation, the name and address of an individual responsible for making the request on behalf of the organisation; (c) the purpose ...; and (d) whether the information will be disclosed to any other person, and if so— (i) ... (ii) ... (iii) ..." (the kinds of person only decide which name and address is meant; the inputs ask for it in whichever form applies)

§§ `s 812 Court supervision of purpose for which rights may be exercised`

DECLARE `s 812(1) what the company must do with the request` IS ONE OF
    `s 812(1)(a) comply with the request`
    `s 812(1)(b) refuse the request`

-- src:10978 | (1) Where a company receives a request under section 811 (register of interests disclosed: right to inspect and require copy), it must—
-- src:10979 | (a) comply with the request if it is satisfied that it is made for a proper purpose, and
-- src:10980 | (b) refuse the request if it is not so satisfied.
@ref s 812(1) Court supervision of purpose for which rights may be exercised (src:10978-10980)
GIVEN `the company is satisfied that the request is made for a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 812(1) what the company must do with the request`
`s 812(1) what the company must do with a request under section 811` MEANS
    IF `the company is satisfied that the request is made for a proper purpose`
    THEN `s 812(1)(a) comply with the request`
    ELSE `s 812(1)(b) refuse the request`

-- src:10981 | (2) If the company refuses the request, it must inform the person making the request, stating the reason why it is not satisfied.
@ref s 812(2) Court supervision of purpose for which rights may be exercised (src:10981-10981)
GIVEN `the company refuses the request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 812(2) the company must inform the person making the request, stating the reason why it is not satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the company refuses the request`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company refuses the request, it must inform the person making the request, stating the reason why it is not satisfied."

-- src:10982 | (3) A person whose request is refused may apply to the court.
@ref s 812(3) Court supervision of purpose for which rights may be exercised (src:10982-10982)
GIVEN `the person's request is refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 812(3) the person may apply to the court` MEANS
    IF `the person's request is refused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person whose request is refused may apply to the court."

-- src:10983 | (4) If an application is made to the court—
-- src:10984 | (a) the person who made the request must notify the company, and
-- src:10985 | (b) the company must use its best endeavours to notify any persons whose details would be disclosed if the company were required to comply with the request.
@ref s 812(4) Court supervision of purpose for which rights may be exercised (src:10983-10985)
GIVEN `an application is made to the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 812(4)(a) the person who made the request must notify the company` MEANS
    IF `an application is made to the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an application is made to the court— (a) the person who made the request must notify the company"

@ref s 812(4)(b) Court supervision of purpose for which rights may be exercised (src:10985-10985)
GIVEN `an application is made to the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 812(4)(b) the company must use its best endeavours to notify any persons whose details would be disclosed` MEANS
    IF `an application is made to the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an application is made to the court— ... (b) the company must use its best endeavours to notify any persons whose details would be disclosed if the company were required to comply with the request."

-- src:10986 | (5) If the court is not satisfied that the inspection or copy is sought for a proper purpose, it shall direct the company not to comply with the request.
@ref s 812(5) Court supervision of purpose for which rights may be exercised (src:10986-10986)
GIVEN `the court is not satisfied that the inspection or copy is sought for a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 812(5) the court shall direct the company not to comply with the request` MEANS
    IF `the court is not satisfied that the inspection or copy is sought for a proper purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court is not satisfied that the inspection or copy is sought for a proper purpose, it shall direct the company not to comply with the request."

-- src:10987 | (6) If the court makes such a direction and it appears to the court that the company is or may be subject to other requests made for a similar purpose (whether made by the same person or different persons), it may direct that the company is not to comply with any such request.
-- src:10988 | The order must contain such provision as appears to the court appropriate to identify the requests to which it applies.
@ref s 812(6) Court supervision of purpose for which rights may be exercised (src:10987-10988)
GIVEN `the court makes a direction under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court that the company is or may be subject to other requests made for a similar purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 812(6) the court may direct that the company is not to comply with any such request` MEANS
    IF `the court makes a direction under subsection (5)` AND `it appears to the court that the company is or may be subject to other requests made for a similar purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court makes such a direction and it appears to the court that the company is or may be subject to other requests made for a similar purpose ..., it may direct that the company is not to comply with any such request.": a grant gated by if; the text is silent on the case where the gate fails (fork F45)

@ref s 812(6) Court supervision of purpose for which rights may be exercised (src:10988-10988)
GIVEN `the order contains such provision as appears to the court appropriate to identify the requests to which it applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 812(6) the order is made as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the order contains such provision as appears to the court appropriate to identify the requests to which it applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The order must contain such provision as appears to the court appropriate to identify the requests to which it applies."

-- src:10989 | (7) If the court does not direct the company not to comply with the request, the company must comply with the request immediately upon the court giving its decision or, as the case may be, the proceedings being discontinued.
@ref s 812(7) Court supervision of purpose for which rights may be exercised (src:10989-10989)
GIVEN `the court does not direct the company not to comply with the request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 812(7) the company must comply with the request immediately upon the court giving its decision or the proceedings being discontinued` MEANS
    IF `the court does not direct the company not to comply with the request`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court does not direct the company not to comply with the request, the company must comply with the request immediately upon the court giving its decision or, as the case may be, the proceedings being discontinued."

§§ `s 813 Register of interests disclosed: refusal of inspection or default in providing copy`

-- src:10991 | (1) If an inspection required under section 811 (register of interests disclosed: right to inspect and require copy) is refused or default is made in providing a copy required under that section, otherwise than in accordance with section 812, an offence is committed by—
-- src:10992 | (a) the company, and
-- src:10993 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 813(1) Register of interests disclosed: refusal of inspection or default in providing copy (src:10991-10993)
GIVEN `an inspection required under section 811 is refused or default is made in providing a copy required under that section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the refusal or default is in accordance with section 812` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 813(1)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `an inspection required under section 811 is refused or default is made in providing a copy required under that section` AND (NOT `the refusal or default is in accordance with section 812`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an inspection required under section 811 ... is refused or default is made in providing a copy required under that section, otherwise than in accordance with section 812, an offence is committed by— (a) the company"

@ref s 813(1)(b) Register of interests disclosed: refusal of inspection or default in providing copy (src:10993-10993)
GIVEN `an inspection required under section 811 is refused or default is made in providing a copy required under that section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the refusal or default is in accordance with section 812` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 813(1)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `an inspection required under section 811 is refused or default is made in providing a copy required under that section` AND (NOT `the refusal or default is in accordance with section 812`)
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default` -- JUST FALSE here is the text's "who is in default"; NOTHING stays NOTHING (points outside the text, s 1121)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "otherwise than in accordance with section 812, an offence is committed by— ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default."

-- src:10994 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 813(2) Register of interests disclosed: refusal of inspection or default in providing copy (src:10994-10994)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 813(2) the penalty on summary conviction` MEANS
    --                         how convicted,                imprisonment not exceeding, fine not exceeding,                                           daily default fine,                                                    imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on summary conviction`                      THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`,                      NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland`          THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`,          NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`  THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`,  NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says only "on summary conviction"; a conviction on indictment is not mentioned

-- src:10995 | (3) In the case of any such refusal or default the court may by order compel an immediate inspection or, as the case may be, direct that the copy required be sent to the person requesting it.
@ref s 813(3) Register of interests disclosed: refusal of inspection or default in providing copy (src:10995-10995)
GIVEN `there is such a refusal or default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 813(3) the court may by order compel an immediate inspection or direct that the copy required be sent to the person requesting it` MEANS
    IF `there is such a refusal or default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of any such refusal or default the court may by order compel an immediate inspection or, as the case may be, direct that the copy required be sent to the person requesting it." ("in the case of" read as "where")

§§ `s 814 Register of interests disclosed: offences in connection with request for or disclosure of information`

-- src:10997 | (1) It is an offence for a person knowingly or recklessly to make in a request under section 811 (register of interests disclosed: right to inspect or require copy) a statement that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular.
@ref s 814(1) Register of interests disclosed: offences in connection with request for or disclosure of information (src:10997-10997)
GIVEN `the person makes in a request under section 811 a statement that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so knowingly or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 814(1) the person commits an offence by a misleading, false or deceptive statement in a request` MEANS
    IF `the person makes in a request under section 811 a statement that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` AND `the person does so knowingly or recklessly`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is an offence for a person knowingly or recklessly to make in a request under section 811 ... a statement that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular": a statement made without knowledge or recklessness is not mentioned

-- src:10998 | (2) It is an offence for a person in possession of information obtained by exercise of either of the rights conferred by that section—
-- src:10999 | (a) to do anything that results in the information being disclosed to another person, or
-- src:11000 | (b) to fail to do anything with the result that the information is disclosed to another person,
-- src:11001 | knowing, or having reason to suspect, that person may use the information for a purpose that is not a proper purpose.
@ref s 814(2) Register of interests disclosed: offences in connection with request for or disclosure of information (src:10998-11001)
GIVEN `the person is in possession of information obtained by exercise of either of the rights conferred by section 811` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does something that results in the information being disclosed to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to do something with the result that the information is disclosed to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows, or has reason to suspect, that the other person may use the information for a purpose that is not a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 814(2) the person commits an offence by disclosing the information` MEANS
    IF     `the person is in possession of information obtained by exercise of either of the rights conferred by section 811`
       AND (   `the person does something that results in the information being disclosed to another person`
            OR `the person fails to do something with the result that the information is disclosed to another person`)
       AND `the person knows, or has reason to suspect, that the other person may use the information for a purpose that is not a proper purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is an offence for a person in possession of information obtained by exercise of either of the rights ... (a) to do anything that results in the information being disclosed ..., or (b) to fail to do anything ..., knowing, or having reason to suspect, that person may use the information for a purpose that is not a proper purpose"

-- src:11002 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:11003 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:11004 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:11005 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:11006 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 814(3) Register of interests disclosed: offences in connection with request for or disclosure of information (src:11002-11006)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 814(3) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    --                         how convicted,                imprisonment not exceeding, fine not exceeding,                                   daily default fine, imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment`                    THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`,                    JUST (Period OF 2, Years),   JUST `a fine without a stated limit`,                  NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales`     THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`,     JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland`              THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`,              JUST (Period OF 6, Months),  JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`      THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`,      JUST (Period OF 6, Months),  JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) on summary conviction— (i) in England and Wales ... (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland": summary conviction is divided by place

§§ `s 815 Entries not to be removed from register`

-- src:11008 | (1) Entries in the register kept under section 808 (register of interests disclosed) must not be deleted except in accordance with—
-- src:11009 | section 816 (old entries), or
-- src:11010 | section 817 (incorrect entry relating to third party).
@ref s 815(1) Entries not to be removed from register (src:11008-11010)
GIVEN `the entry is deleted in accordance with section 816 (old entries)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entry is deleted in accordance with section 817 (incorrect entry relating to third party)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 815(1) the deletion of the entry is permitted` MEANS
    IF `the entry is deleted in accordance with section 816 (old entries)` OR `the entry is deleted in accordance with section 817 (incorrect entry relating to third party)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Entries in the register kept under section 808 ... must not be deleted except in accordance with— section 816 (old entries), or section 817 (incorrect entry relating to third party)."

-- src:11011 | (2) If an entry is deleted in contravention of subsection (1), the company must restore it as soon as reasonably practicable.
@ref s 815(2) Entries not to be removed from register (src:11011-11011)
GIVEN `an entry is deleted in contravention of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 815(2) the company must restore the entry as soon as reasonably practicable` MEANS
    IF `an entry is deleted in contravention of subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an entry is deleted in contravention of subsection (1), the company must restore it as soon as reasonably practicable."

@ref s 815(2) Entries not to be removed from register (src:11011-11011)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 815(2) the company must restore an entry deleted in contravention of subsection (1)` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST (`Action of a party` OF Company, Company, "s 815(2) restores the entry that was deleted in contravention of subsection (1)")
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 815(2): the entry deleted in contravention of subsection (1) was not restored"

-- src:11012 | (3) If default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (2), an offence is committed by—
-- src:11013 | (a) the company, and
-- src:11014 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 815(3) Entries not to be removed from register (src:11012-11014)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 815(3)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (2), an offence is committed by— (a) the company"

@ref s 815(3)(b) Entries not to be removed from register (src:11014-11014)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 815(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (2)`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default` -- JUST FALSE here is the text's "who is in default"; NOTHING stays NOTHING (points outside the text, s 1121)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (2), an offence is committed by— ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default."

-- src:11015 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention of subsection (2), a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 815(4) Entries not to be removed from register (src:11015-11015)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `the contravention is a continued contravention of subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 815(4) the penalty on summary conviction` MEANS
    --                         how convicted,                imprisonment not exceeding, fine not exceeding,                                           daily default fine,                                                                                    imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on summary conviction`                      THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`,                      NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), IF `the contravention is a continued contravention of subsection (2)` THEN JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1) ELSE NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), IF `the contravention is a continued contravention of subsection (2)` THEN JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1) ELSE NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland`          THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`,          NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), IF `the contravention is a continued contravention of subsection (2)` THEN JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1) ELSE NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`  THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`,  NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), IF `the contravention is a continued contravention of subsection (2)` THEN JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1) ELSE NOTHING, FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says only "on summary conviction"; a conviction on indictment is not mentioned

§§ `s 816 Removal of entries from register: old entries`

-- src:11016 | 816 Removal of entries from register: old entries
-- src:11017 | A company may remove an entry from the register kept under section 808 (register of interests disclosed) if more than six years have elapsed since the entry was made.
@ref s 816 Removal of entries from register: old entries (src:11016-11017)
GIVEN `the date on which the entry was made` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 816 the company may remove the entry from the register` MEANS
    IF Day `the date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN Day (`add years` `the date on which the entry was made` 6)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company may remove an entry from the register kept under section 808 ... if more than six years have elapsed since the entry was made.": a grant gated by if; the text is silent on the case where the gate fails (fork F46)

§§ `s 817 Removal of entries from register: incorrect entry relating to third party`

-- src:11019 | (1) This section applies where in pursuance of an obligation imposed by a notice under section 793 (notice requiring information about interests in company's shares) a person gives to a company the name and address of another person as being interested in shares in the company.
@ref s 817(1) Removal of entries from register: incorrect entry relating to third party (src:11019-11019)
