GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 817(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `in pursuance of an obligation imposed by a notice under section 793 a person gives to the company the name and address of another person as being interested in shares in the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where in pursuance of an obligation imposed by a notice under section 793 ... a person gives to a company the name and address of another person as being interested in shares in the company."

-- src:11020 | (2) That other person may apply to the company for the removal of the entry from the register.
@ref s 817(2) Removal of entries from register: incorrect entry relating to third party (src:11020-11020)
GIVEN `this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 817(2) that other person may apply to the company for the removal of the entry from the register` MEANS
    IF `this section applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
