§§ `s 819 Duty of company ceasing to be public company`

-- src:11029 | 819 Duty of company ceasing to be public company
-- src:11030 | (1) If a company ceases to be a public company, it must continue to keep any register kept under section 808 (register of interests disclosed), and any associated index, until the end of the period of six years after it ceased to be such a company.
@ref s 819(1) Duty of company ceasing to be public company (src:11029-11030)
GIVEN `the company ceases to be a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which it ceased to be a public company` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 819(1) the company must continue to keep the register and any associated index` MEANS
    IF `the company ceases to be a public company`
    THEN IF Day `the date on which the question is asked` AT MOST Day (`add years` `the date on which it ceased to be a public company` 6)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the end of the period of six years after it ceased to be such a company"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company ceases to be a public company, it must continue to keep any register"

